    "long_instructions": "# Explore Documentation\r\n\r\nYour code can already print a message ... but what else can `print()` do?\r\n\r\nCan you make it show two messages on one line? Add a blank line? Show numbers and text together? \r\n\r\n# Try It (with AI Tutor)\r\n\r\nUse the AI Tutor to **explore the documentation for the `print()` command.**\r\n\r\nYou can click the \"Show documentation\" button or ask questions like:\r\n* _What does the `print()` function do in Python?_\r\n* _What are some examples of `print()` with different arguments?_\r\n\r\n***Tip: Copy an example from the Tutor and try it in your code to see what happens!***",
