    "teacher_markdown": "This level is not about memorizing arguments; it’s about learning to look up and experiment.\r\n\r\nEmphasize that programmers rarely remember everything — they use documentation and AI tools.\r\n\r\nEncourage students to describe one new thing they learned about `print()` from the Tutor.",
    "additional_ai_evaluation_instructions": "The goal of this level is for students to practice using the AI Tutor to explore documentation and examples. \r\nIf the student's code runs and demonstrates a new use of the `print()` function learned from documentation, \r\nconsider it correct even if formatting or punctuation is not perfect. \r\nPrioritize whether the student applied new knowledge from the AI Tutor rather than how advanced the code is.\r\n",
